# Code owners for NKE Recipes.
#
# GitHub requests review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so the default is declared first and the
# trust roots override it below.
#
# Every path currently resolves to @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write. The path list below is
# retained deliberately: it records which files are trust roots — anything that
# determines WHAT GETS BUILT, WHAT IS TRUSTED, or WHAT RUNS IN CI — so that
# tightening them later is a change of owner on known lines rather than a fresh
# analysis.
#
# Why not @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-maintainer today: that team is org-wide (18 people, only
# two of whom work on this repository), so routing trust roots there requests
# review from people with no context while excluding contributors who have it.
# An NKE-Recipes-scoped team does not exist at the org level. Revisit when one
# does.
#
# Roles are defined in GOVERNANCE.md. The team must hold write access to this
# repository or GitHub silently ignores the entry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — all trusted contributors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*                                       @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trust roots — same owner as the default today; tighten here when a
# repository-scoped team exists
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The lock contract (ADR-22). A lock entry is the exact content identity of
# something that will be built and published; changing one changes what ships.
/definitions/**/catalog/pins.lock.yaml  @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# The registry: which components exist and their constraints. Paired with the
# lock above under ADR-22's registry/lockfile split.
/definitions/**/catalog/registry.yaml   @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# Definition and Environment are Tier-1 inputs bound into `recipeDigest`
# (ADR-11, ADR-12). A change here changes recipe identity.
/definitions/**/definition.yaml         @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/definitions/**/environment-*.yaml      @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# Toolchain pins. A toolchain digest is a build-semantic input (ADR-10 §5) and
# contaminates every artifact built with it.
/toolchains/**/*.lock.json              @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# The design record. ADRs govern design and are what a change is reviewed
# against; amending one is amending the contract.
/docs/adr/                              @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# CI, workflows, and repository automation. This is the code that decides what
# "passing" means, plus the generated Run pipeline and its plan.
/.github/                               @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# The CI contract: `make check` is what CI runs, so a Makefile change changes
# the gate.
/Makefile                               @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# Dependency surface. CONTRIBUTING names Apache-cleanliness a load-bearing
# invariant, and it is enforced here by review until a license gate exists.
/go.mod                                 @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/go.sum                                 @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write

# Licensing, security policy, governance, and this file.
/LICENSE                                @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/SECURITY.md                            @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/GOVERNANCE.md                          @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/MAINTAINERS.md                         @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                     @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @dsx-ai-factory/nvke-write
